  "marketSentiment": "NEUTRAL",
  "macroTheme": "Fed Chair Warsh's hawkish Jackson Hole debut transforms September FOMC into a live meeting; price stability declared 'predominant focus.' Gold crushed 3.7% as debasement trade unwinds. NVDA beat ($96.22B) keeps AI bid intact. Equities resilient but breadth narrow — Russell 2000 -1.5%.",
  "macroOverview": "The week ending 28 August was defined by a violent collision between the AI trade and a hawkish Fed reality check. NVDA delivered a standout quarter ($96.22B revenue, ~70% annual growth guide) that sent the stock up 8.7% and kept the Nasdaq positive. But Warsh's Jackson Hole address on Friday — declaring price stability the Fed's 'predominant focus' and keeping rate hikes on the table — shattered the precious-metals debasement trade and sent gold crashing from 4,688 to 4,495 intraday. Equities held up (Dow +0.53%, S&P +0.49%, Nasdaq +0.85%) but breadth was terrifyingly narrow with the Russell 2000 falling 1.5%. Core PCE printed 3.3% YoY — sticky above target. The week ahead is dominated by ISM PMIs, Broadcom earnings, BoC/RBNZ rate decisions, and the August employment report on Friday.",
